    "title": "UConn vs Duke schedule, TV channel, how to watch Elite 8 game Sunday",
    "text": "March 27, 2026Updated March 28, 2026, 8:33 a.m. MTNo. 1 seed Duke and No. 2 seed UConn play in a March Madness NCAA Tournament Elite Eight men's college basketball game on Sunday, March 29.Here's what to know about the time, TV channel, streaming information and announcers for the East Region March Madness Elite Eight game.Duke advanced to this game with wins over Siena, TCU and St. John's.UConn beat Furman, UCLA and Michigan State.The winner of this game will advance to the Final Four of the NCAA Tournament on Saturday, April 4.How to watch Elite 8 games: Iowa vs Illinois | Purdue vs Arizona | Tennessee vs Michigan | UConn vs Duke | Schedule | Announcers | Who is in Elite 8?Watch Duke vs UConn on FUBO (free trial)What time is the UConn vs Duke March Madness game?The Duke vs UConn NCAA Tournament Elite Eight game is scheduled for 2:05 p.m. MST (5:05 p.m. ET) on Sunday, March 29.What channel is the Duke vs UConn March Madness game on?The UConn vs Duke Elite Eight NCAA Tournament game can be seen on CBS.March Madness Elite 8 picks: Iowa vs Illinois | Purdue vs Arizona | Tennessee vs Michigan | UConn vs Duke | The Republic's predictionsHow can I stream the UConn vs Duke March Madness game?Duke vs UConn can be streamed on FUBO and other streaming services that carry CBS. FUBO offers a free trial.Who are the announcers for the Duke vs UConn March Madness game?Ian Eagle will have the play-by-play call of the UConn Huskies vs Duke Blue Devils NCAA Tournament game, with Robbie Hummel and Stan Van Gundy as the analysts and Tracy Wolfson as the reporter for the March Madness Elite Eight matchup.March Madness Elite 8 odds: Iowa vs Illinois | Purdue vs Arizona | Tennessee vs Michigan | UConn vs Duke | Betting odds | National championship oddsReach Jeremy Cluff at jeremy.cluff@arizonarepublic.com. Follow him on X, formerly Twitter @Jeremy_Cluff.Support local journalism: Subscribe to azcentral.com today. Sign up for azcentral Preps Now. And be sure to subscribe to our daily sports newsletters so you don't miss a thing.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
